globalThis.pzCourseExport="# CranRich · course dossier\n\nRevision: Revision 80\ncourse:04457c8b-3d82-5318-afe6-8aeaa048a88c\ndocumented_course\n2025-02-22 · Estimated end 2025-05-22 · The patient estimates about three months after the February 22 CranRich start, or roughly May 2025. Individual dosing during the March hospital interruption is unclear.\nDate-window anchor: Recorded course start · 2025-02-22\n\n## Baseline before the selected anchor\n\n- 2025-01-03 · Selected activities became possible during better windows · He tolerated some classical music but described worsened burning or fog with much other music. He was frequently bedridden and too weak for consistent notes. He later recalled being able to leave the dark room for the first half of the day after January 8, with PEM and burning still recurring. · winter dark-room state · An individual response could vary by day, intervention or activity. The duration of the improvement is uncertain.\n  Source · baseline_states:BL-12\n\n## Intended targets\n\n- renal_urinary · S3:648 | The history specifies recent urinary tract symptoms as the reason for cranberry extract.\n  Source · intervention_events:S3:T:648:1\n\n## Actions and doses\n\n- 2025-02-22 · Start · twice daily\n  Source · 2025-02-22 · start · twice daily · consecutive_sequence_aligned_to_dated_posts · reported_use · primary · S1:23041–23055 · [intervention_events:S1-C23041-1] | 2025-02-22 · start · day · source_account · corroborating · S3:648–648 · [intervention_events:S3:T:648:1]\n\n## Course timing evidence\n\n- 2025-03-25 · hold day · The March 25 diary reports stopping all supplements for the hospital visit. The date this individual supplement resumed is unconfirmed.\n  Source · diary_fields:S1-L29796-FL4\n- 2025-05 · estimated end · The patient estimates about three months after the February 22 CranRich start, or roughly May 2025. Individual dosing during the March hospital interruption is unclear.\n  Source · pz_review57_course:course:04457c8b-3d82-5318-afe6-8aeaa048a88c\n- 2025-05-22 · estimated end anchor · About 3 calendar months from 2025-02-22, using the duration in the patient review. The exact last dose is unknown.\n  Source · pz_review57_course:course:04457c8b-3d82-5318-afe6-8aeaa048a88c\n- 2026-11-20 · stopped by · Confirmed off the regimen by this date. Exact last dose unknown.\n  Source · pz_regimen_snapshot:PZ-STACK-2026-11-20\n\n## Potential effects\n\nNo linked record at this scope.\n\n## Potential effects reported outside a specific course\n\nNo linked record at this scope.\n\n## Source evidence and qualifications\n\n- [archive_messages:S1-M11354] · reported 2025-01-05T08:07:59+01:00 · We should definitely note down skipped doses · researcher commentary · 2025-01-05T08:07:59+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M11358] · reported 2025-01-05T08:10:07+01:00 · are you taking notes? i can try (i used to) but these days i'm too weak and too often bedridden to be consistent at it · patient account or question · 2025-01-05T08:10:07+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M12902] · reported 2025-01-12T22:17:22+01:00 · update#5: - 'narcoleptic' early sleep last night, 7pm-3.30am - BP=129/104, HR=79 - some hand tingling/coldness - later feet cold - bad burns briefly around breakfast then around lunch. maybe some correlation with KPV? - some gut pain, there was Chinese kale in my meal, maybe that? also, i eat a lot of broccoli and apparently it contains some sulfur - basically despite stopping L-cysteine 3d ago, L-ornithine today, there is no difference in burns, maybe a bit more today - pre-PEM back of head pain onset at 5.30-6 - went to rest in dark room and mostly disappeared. got up and reappeared but didn't appear to be progressing into pem, just a low grade ache in back of head - def a lot hungrier today, ate more than usual too (since you asked) - 2x bm · patient account or question · 2025-01-12T22:17:22+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M23041] · reported 2025-02-23T13:55:03+01:00 · update#40: - rating (1-10): 1.5 - sleep (following day): not great, woke too early due to urination urge, as usual - PEM: woke w mild; mild-mod crash in morning/noon; crash-y all afternoon w/ bad back of head pain - narcolepsy: 0 - burns: mild-mod (overshadowed by PEM) - tinnitus: sev - POTS: mild - stool: 1x normal - gut pain: mild flare again - hunger: less than usual - activity: mild - UTI: mild sx - cold/heat: usual - changes: started CranRich 2x/day; restart Magtein (was out for a while); 9g glycine instead of 6g · patient message · 2025-02-23T13:55:03+01:00\n- [baseline_states:BL-12] · 2025-01-03 · through 2025-01-12 · Selected activities became possible during better windows · He tolerated some classical music but described worsened burning or fog with much other music. He was frequently bedridden and too weak for consistent notes. He later recalled being able to leave the dark room for the first half of the day after January 8, with PEM and burning still recurring. · winter dark-room state · An individual response could vary by day, intervention or activity. The duration of the improvement is uncertain.\n- [diary_fields:S1-L29796-FL4] · 2025-03-25 · changes · hospital visit; stopped all supplements · as labelled\n- [diary_logs:S1-L29796] · 2025-03-25 · reported 2025-03-26T11:55:47+01:00 · update#71: - rating (1-10): 2 - sleep (following day): absolutely terrible, was up more than i was asleep it felt like - PEM: pem in pm after tests and talking to ppl - narcolepsy: - burns/pressures: - tinnitus: - POTS: - stool: 2x in morning one after another - gut pain: - hunger: - activity: - cold/heat: - changes: hospital visit; stopped all supplements · previous_day_reporting_convention · 2025-03-26T11:55:47+01:00\n- [intervention_events:S1-C23041-1] · 2025-02-22 · reported 2025-02-23T13:55:03+01:00 · CranRich · start · twice daily · consecutive_sequence_aligned_to_dated_posts · reported_use · primary\n- [intervention_events:S3:T:648:1] · 2025-02-22 · CranRich · start · day · source_account · corroborating\n- [s1_quote_context:S1-M11358#1] · reported 2025-01-05T08:10:07+01:00 · unverified; see linked parent where identified\n- [source_lines:S3:617] · * 8:\n- [source_lines:S3:618] · * ▶️ Arterosil: increase NO, anticoagulant, anti-plaque, reduces vascular inflammation\n- [source_lines:S3:619] · * ▶️ glutathione 2x250-500mg: since OAT shows impaired synthesis → relief in PEM, since then able to leave dark room for first half of day (previously spent most of the day in bed)\n- [source_lines:S3:620] · * 9: ▶️ L-carnitine 3x4.5g: suspicion of carnitine theft by Candida (as per OAT) → slightly less PEM and higher body temperature, hands/feet not cold anymore\n- [source_lines:S3:621] · * stopped after 1 month → mild improvement probably confirms beta-oxidation issue but it’s not the main problem\n- [treatment_intervals:EARLY-I-S1-C23041-1] · 2025-02-22 · CranRich · 2025-02-22 · hospital_changes_interrupt_observation · Use before the March 25 hospital medication/supplement interruption; exact end unknown. · primary";
